t settlement in the shadow of luxury hotels near the Mumbai airport, and as India starts to prosper, Annawadians are electric with hope. Abdul, a reflective and enterprising Muslim teenager, sees fortune in the recyclable garbage of richer people. Asha, a woman of formidable wit and deep scars from a rural childhood, has identified an alternate route to the middle class: political corruption. With a little luck, her sensitive, beautiful daughter, Annawadi's \"most-everything girl,\" will soon become its first female college graduate. And even the poorest Annawadians, like Kalu, a fifteen-year-old scrap metal thief, believe themselves inching closer to good times they call \"the full enjoy.\" But then Abdul the garbage sorter is falsely accused in a shocking tragedy; terror and a global recession rock the city; and suppressed tensions over religion, caste, sex, power and economic envy turn brutal.","pageCount":256,"subjectCategories":[{"source":"open_library","scheme":"open_library_subject","label":"Urban poor","sourceId":"source-open-library-behind-the-beautiful-forevers-life-death-and-hope-in-a-mumbai-undercity-katherine-boo"},{"source":"open_library","scheme":"open_library_subject","label":"New York Times bestseller","sourceId":"source-open-library-behind-the-beautiful-forevers-life-death-and-hope-in-a-mumbai-undercity-katherine-boo"},{"source":"open_library","scheme":"open_library_subject","label":"Creative nonfiction","sourceId":"source-open-library-behind-the-beautiful-forevers-life-death-and-hope-in-a-mumbai-undercity-katherine-boo"},{"source":"open_library","scheme":"open_library_subject","label":"nyt:hardcover_political_books=2012-02-25","sourceId":"source-open-library-behind-the-beautiful-forevers-life-death-and-hope-in-a-mumbai-undercity-katherine-boo"},{"source":"open_library","scheme":"open_library_subject","label":"Poor","sourceId":"source-open-library-behind-the-beautiful-forevers-life-death-and-hope-in-a-mumbai-undercity-katherine-boo"},{"source":"ope