 years of reporting, a bewildering age of global change and inequality is made human. The events recounted are real, as are all the names. Annawadi is a makeshift settlement in the shadow of luxury hotels near the Mumbai airport, and as India starts to prosper, Annawadians are electric with hope. Abdul, a reflective and enterprising Muslim teenager, sees fortune in the recyclable garbage of richer people. Asha, a woman of formidable wit and deep scars from a rural childhood, has identified an alternate route to the middle class: political corruption. With a little luck, her sensitive, beautiful daughter, Annawadi's \"most-everything girl,\" will soon become its first female college graduate. And even the poorest Annawadians, like Kalu, a fifteen-year-old scrap metal thief, believe themselves inching closer to good times they call \"the full enjoy.\" But then Abdul the garbage sorter is falsely accused in a shocking tragedy; terror and a global recession rock the city; and suppressed tensions over religion, caste, sex, power and economic envy turn brutal.","primaryTopic":"Housing, Cities & Urban Life","subjectEvidence":{"primarySubject":"Society & Culture","confidence":"high","method":"evidence_score","candidates":[{"subject":"Society & Culture","score":8,"evidenceCount":1}],"evidence":[{"source":"llm_classifier","rawLabel":"Society & Culture","mappedSubject":"Society & Culture","score":8,"confidence":"high","note":"The book primarily explores the social conditions and struggles of families in Mumbai's underclass, while also addressing economic factors and being a work of narrative journalism.","id":"subject-evidence-book-behind-the-beautiful-forevers-life-death-and-hope-in-a-mumbai-undercity-katherine-boo-1"},{"source":"open_library","scheme":"open_library_subject","rawLabel":"Poverty","mappedSubject":"Society & Culture","score":5,"confidence":"high","sourceId":"source-open-library-behind-the-beautiful-forevers-life-death-and-hope-in-a-mumbai-undercity-katherine-boo