 an intimate portrait of poverty, inequality, and resilience in modern India. Drawing from three years of immersive reporting, Boo explores the impacts of globalization, corruption, and social dynamics through the stories of several families. Behind the Beautiful Forevers received widespread critical acclaim and won the National Book Award for Nonfiction in 2012. It was later adapted into a play by David Hare that premiered at the National Theatre in London.","matchedBy":"infobox_book:high","confidence":"high","attribution":{"label":"Wikipedia","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Behind_the_Beautiful_Forevers","license":"CC BY-SA","licenseUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/"},"infobox":{"title":"Behind the Beautiful Forevers","author":"Katherine Boo","publisher":"Random House","publicationDate":"2012","publicationPlace":"United States","pages":"256 pp.","isbn":"978-1-4000-6755-8","language":"English","subject":"Poverty, inequality, corruption in India","genre":"Non-fiction"},"publisherEvidenceId":"publisher-evidence-wikipedia-behind-the-beautiful-forevers-life-death-and-hope-in-a-mumbai-undercity-katherine-boo"},"sources":[{"id":"source-award-record-carnegie-nonfiction-ala-carnegie-medals-2013-annual-page","label":"ALA Carnegie Medals 2013 annual page","url":"https://www.ala.org/carnegie-medals/2013-winners","accessedAt":"2026-07-22T05:31:21.119Z","confidence":"official","field":"award","note":"Official awards URL: https://www.ala.org/rusa/awards/carnegie-medals"},{"id":"source-award-record-dayton-nonfiction-wikipedia-dayton-literary-peace-prize-nonfiction-table","label":"Wikipedia: Dayton Literary Peace Prize nonfiction table","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dayton_Literary_Peace_Prize","accessedAt":"2026-07-22T05:31:21.119Z","confidence":"secondary","field":"award","note":"Official awards URL: https://www.daytonliterarypeaceprize.org/"},{"id":"source-award-record-helen-bernstein-journalism-wikipedia-helen-bernstein-book-award-for-excellence